/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An air standard analysis rests on four assumptions.
   - With these four, the cycle is a loop on the p-v and T-s diagrams, and the heat and work of each process follow from first-law formulas.
   - η = wnet/qin = 1 − qout/qin
   - Here wnet is the net work per kg of air in one cycle, qin is the heat added and qout the heat rejected, all in kJ/kg.
   - Four kinds of process build all the cycles of this unit.
   - On a T-s diagram an isentropic process is a vertical line and an isothermal process a horizontal line.
   - The Carnot gas cycle takes in all its heat at the highest temperature TH and rejects all of it at the lowest temperature TL.
   - The two isentropic steps have the same temperature ratio, so v₄/v₁ = v₃/v₂ and the logarithms cancel in qout/qin.
   - ηCarnot = 1 − TL/TH
   - No engine between the same two temperatures can beat it (Carnot's theorem), yet no engine runs on it, for three reasons.
*/
