/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - State 1 is the start of compression.
   - ηOtto = 1 − 1/rγ−1.
   - The Diesel cycle keeps 1→2 isentropic compression, 3→4 isentropic expansion and 4→1 constant-volume rejection, but heat goes in at constant pressure from 2 to 3.
   - ηDiesel = 1 − (1/rγ−1) × (rcγ − 1)/[γ(rc − 1)].
   - The Dual (mixed, or limited-pressure) cycle has five processes: 1→2 isentropic compression, 2→3 heat at constant volume, 3→4 heat at constant pressure, 4→5 isentropic expansion and 5→1 rejection at constant volume.
   - qin = cv(T₃ − T₂) + cp(T₄ − T₃), qout = cv(T₅ − T₁), with T₃ = rpT₂, T₄ = rcT₃ and T₅ = T₁rprcγ.
   - ηDual = 1 − (1/rγ−1) × (rprcγ − 1)/[(rp − 1) + γrp(rc − 1)]
   - Put rc = 1 and the formula becomes the Otto formula; put rp = 1 and it becomes the Diesel formula.
*/
