/* book Worked example 2: Q: An air standard Diesel cycle has a compression ratio of 15, and fuel cut-off occurs at 6% of the stroke. The air is at 1 bar and 300 K at the start of compression. Take cp = 1.005 and cv = 0.718 kJ/kg·K, γ = 1.4. Find the cut-off ratio, the temperatures, the heat added and rejected, and the efficiency.
   1. Cut-off ratio: rc = 1 + 0.06 × (15 − 1) = 1.84.
   2. T₂ = 300 × 150.4 = 300 × 2.954 = 886.3 K; p₂ = 151.4 = 44.31 bar.
   3. T₃ = rcT₂ = 1.84 × 886.3 = 1630.7 K. T₄ = T₁rcγ = 300 × 1.841.4 = 300 × 2.348 = 704.5 K.
   4. qin = 1.005 × (1630.7 − 886.3) = 748.2 kJ/kg; qout = 0.718 × (704.5 − 300) = 290.4 kJ/kg.
   5. wnet = 748.2 − 290.4 = 457.8 kJ/kg, so η = 457.8/748.2 = 0.612.
   6. Check with the formula: 1 − (1/2.954) × (2.348 − 1)/(1.4 × 0.84) = 1 − 0.3385 × 1.146 = 0.612.
   Answer: rc = 1.84; T₂ = 886.3 K, T₃ = 1630.7 K, T₄ = 704.5 K; qin = 748.2 kJ/kg, qout = 290.4 kJ/kg; η = 61.2%. */
